      "message": "I actually think the CID could/should be identified by VS. As a binder service, it should be able to know the peer address of a transaction. (similar to getCallingPid/Uid for local binder transactions). Unfortunately, such mechanism doesn\u0027t exist yet, better to file a bug to smoreland@.\n\nIn the meantime, you could create a bind socket temporarily and call https://docs.rs/vsock/0.1.4/vsock/struct.VsockListener.html#method.local_addr on it to get the CID of the current VM. My point is that you don\u0027t need to take the difficult path of using ioctl.",
